  <title>Table navigation</title>
  <p>
    Table navigation lets you use Orca commands to move by cell, row, and column in tables.
  </p>
  <p>
    Table navigation is not limited to document content. It can also be used in application
    tables. To move among tables in document content, use structural navigation. Table
    navigation moves within the current table and remains available in both browse mode and
    focus mode.
  </p>
  <p>
    Some tables do not expose their headers to assistive technologies, such as a text document
    or spreadsheet where headers are only visually formatted as bold cells. The dynamic-header
    commands below let you identify those headers.
  </p>
  <section id="settings-table-navigation">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Documents</gui> category, <gui>Table navigation</gui> group.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Table navigation</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca's table navigation commands are available. Default: on.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Skip blank cells</gui>: Controls whether
          table navigation skips empty cells. Default: off.
        </p>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
  <section id="commands-table-navigation">
    <title>Commands</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Commands</gui> category, <gui>Commands</gui> section, <gui>Table navigation</gui> group.
    </p>
    <section id="table-navigation-navigation">
      <title>Navigation</title>
      <list>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Toggle table navigation keys</gui>: <keyseq>
              <key>Orca Modifier</key>
              <key>Shift</key>
              <key>T</key>
            </keyseq>
          </p>
          <p>
            Turns Orca's table navigation commands on or off.
          </p>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Go left one cell</gui>: <keyseq>
              <key>Alt</key>
              <key>Shift</key>
              <key>Left Arrow</key>
            </keyseq>
          </p>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Go right one cell</gui>: <keyseq>
              <key>Alt</key>
              <key>Shift</key>
              <key>Right Arrow</key>
            </keyseq>
          </p>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Go up one cell</gui>: <keyseq>
              <key>Alt</key>
              <key>Shift</key>
              <key>Up Arrow</key>
            </keyseq>
          </p>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Go down one cell</gui>: <keyseq>
              <key>Alt</key>
              <key>Shift</key>
              <key>Down Arrow</key>
            </keyseq>
          </p>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Go to the first cell in a table</gui>: <keyseq>
              <key>Alt</key>
              <key>Shift</key>
              <key>Home</key>
            </keyseq>
          </p>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Go to the last cell in a table</gui>: <keyseq>
              <key>Alt</key>
              <key>Shift</key>
              <key>End</key>
            </keyseq>
          </p>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Go to the beginning of the row</gui>: <keyseq>
              <key>Orca Modifier</key>
              <key>Alt</key>
              <key>Shift</key>
              <key>Left Arrow</key>
            </keyseq>
          </p>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Go to the end of the row</gui>: <keyseq>
              <key>Orca Modifier</key>
              <key>Alt</key>
              <key>Shift</key>
              <key>Right Arrow</key>
            </keyseq>
          </p>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Go to the top of the column</gui>: <keyseq>
              <key>Orca Modifier</key>
              <key>Alt</key>
              <key>Shift</key>
              <key>Up Arrow</key>
            </keyseq>
          </p>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Go to the bottom of the column</gui>: <keyseq>
              <key>Orca Modifier</key>
              <key>Alt</key>
              <key>Shift</key>
              <key>Down Arrow</key>
            </keyseq>
          </p>
        </item>
      </list>
    </section>
    <section id="table-navigation-dynamic-headers">
      <title>Dynamic headers</title>
      <list>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Set the row to use as dynamic column headers</gui>: <keyseq>
              <key>Orca Modifier</key>
              <key>Shift</key>
              <key>R</key>
            </keyseq>
          </p>
          <p>
            Marks the current row as column headers for the table. First move to the row
            containing the headers. Orca presents those headers as you navigate, announcing them
            when they change rather than repeating them for every cell with the same header.
          </p>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Clear the dynamic column headers</gui>: <keyseq>
              <key>Orca Modifier</key>
              <key>Shift</key>
              <key>R</key>
            </keyseq>
            (press twice quickly)
          </p>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Set the column to use as dynamic row headers</gui>: <keyseq>
              <key>Orca Modifier</key>
              <key>Shift</key>
              <key>C</key>
            </keyseq>
          </p>
          <p>
            Marks the current column as row headers for the table. First move to the column
            containing the headers. Orca presents those headers as you navigate, announcing them
            when they change rather than repeating them for every cell with the same header.
          </p>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Clear the dynamic row headers</gui>: <keyseq>
              <key>Orca Modifier</key>
              <key>Shift</key>
              <key>C</key>
            </keyseq>
            (press twice quickly)
          </p>
        </item>
      </list>
    </section>
  </section>
